Subject: d3d11on12: give the upload-heap submit trigger a real limit

D3D12TranslationLayer submits a command list early once the upload space
allocated since the last submit exceeds a limit, so that recycled upload
memory is not held hostage by a long command list. CommandListManager sets
that limit to min(cMaxAllocatedUploadHeapSpacePerCommandList, which is
256 MB, and CreationArgs::MaxAllocatedUploadHeapSpacePerCommandList).

GetImmCtxArgs never sets the field, and CreationArgs zero-initialises
itself, so the limit here is zero. Unlike MaxSRVHeapSize, which DTL treats
as "use the default" when zero, nothing maps zero back: every upload --
a dynamic constant buffer update before a draw is enough -- makes the next
PostRender submit whenever the GPU is idle. On this target that is a
command-list close, ExecuteCommandLists into D3DMetal and a fresh list per
draw, which is the CPU cost the batching exists to avoid.

MAXDWORD defers to DTL's own 256 MB rather than restating it: its
constant is private to CommandListManager, and the min() already picks it.
---
diff --git a/src/device.cpp b/src/device.cpp
index 1190d04..d999744 100644
--- a/src/device.cpp
+++ b/src/device.cpp
@@ -271,6 +271,9 @@ namespace D3D11On12
         args.UseResidencyManagement = true;
         args.DisableGPUTimeout = pAdapter->m_bAPIDisablesGPUTimeout;
         args.IsXbox = IsXboxCreateFlags(CreateDeviceFlags);
+        // CommandListManager caps this at min(its own 256 MB, this field); a
+        // zero here would make every upload trigger a submit.
+        args.MaxAllocatedUploadHeapSpacePerCommandList = MAXDWORD;
 #ifdef __D3D11On12CreatorID_INTERFACE_DEFINED__
         args.CreatorID = uuidof<D3D11On12CreatorID>();
 #endif
